<http://data.silknow.org/object/2bd56adb-6009-3f19-aafd-881bb2a27215/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Shawl of printed wool and silk gauze with bands of additional silk warp and weft that are wide in the borders and narrow to mark off large squares in the centre. Deep maroon colour with a wide border printed in maroon, yellow, pink, blue, green and white. Small flower-filled cones are outlined in twisted cable to project into the maroon centre, alternating with fantastic motifs.  They are based on a border made up of five main stripes, and the centre one has a broken cone form and the other four are filled with a twisting rope with what locks like a triple fungus at intervals. The two shorter sides of the shawl have a fringe of maroon silk."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/2bd56adb-6009-3f19-aafd-881bb2a27215> .

